Qt 6 does not ship a QML module named QtGui. ecm_add_qml_module
DEPENDENCIES QtGui still writes "depends QtGui" into the embedded
qmldir. The QML engine does not load that line; qmlimportscanner
and the RPM generator do. Nothing provides qml(QtGui), so
plasma-setup cannot be installed. No QML type here exposes a QtGui
class, and the QML files do not import QtGui.

diff -up plasma-setup-6.8.2/src/CMakeLists.txt.qtgui plasma-setup-6.8.2/src/CMakeLists.txt
--- plasma-setup-6.8.2/src/CMakeLists.txt.qtgui	2026-10-27 12:31:00.000000000 +0100
+++ plasma-setup-6.8.2/src/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-08 22:10:00.000000000 +0100
@@ -33,8 +33,7 @@ add_executable(plasma-setup
 
 ecm_add_qml_module(plasma-setup GENERATE_PLUGIN_SOURCE
     URI "org.kde.plasmasetup"
-    DEPENDENCIES
-        QtGui
+    DEPENDENCIES
         QtQuick
 )
 
